      "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0768221924b6a280817a6a992a248cdc1bb66e8e.001.1",
      "event": "High Surf Advisory",
      "severity": "Minor",
      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 11 at 3:43AM HST until November 12 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH AND WEST FACING SHORES OF NIIHAU\nKAUAI OAHU MOLOKAI AND NORTH FACING SHORES OF MAUI...\n\n.Surf heights will build through the day, peaking tonight and\nnear-warning level surf may linger into Thursday, with surf\nfalling below advisory levels by Thursday night.\n\n* WHAT...For north-facing shores, surf increasing to 15 to 20 feet\ntoday, peaking at 18 to 24 feet tonight, possibly into Thursday\nmorning, then diminishing through Thursday. For west-facing\nshores, surf increasing to 10 to 15 feet today, peaking at 14 to\n18 feet tonight, then diminishing through Thursday.\n\n* WHERE...North and west facing shores of Niihau, Kauai, Oahu,\nMolokai and north facing shores of Maui.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM HST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
      "instruction": "Heed all advice from ocean safety officials. When in doubt, don't\ngo out.",
      "areaDesc": "Niihau; Waianae Coast; Oahu North Shore; Maui Windward West; Kauai North; Molokai Windward; Molokai North; Molokai West; Maui Central Valley North; Windward Haleakala",
